  "description": "Royal blue from the nose back to just ahead of the tail's red sweep, with a thin white line between them and the white tail cone behind; 'Emirates' in red instead of gold between the decks; aft of it a white outline basketball bouncing aft in three white arcs, 'Official Airline Partner of the NBA' in small white lettering and the NBA's logo (the red, white and blue logoman) over the wing root. Red engine cowlings with the calligraphy logo in white; the 2023 scheme's flag tail, red sweep and red winglets.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.emirates.com/media-centre/emirates-introduces-bold-nba-livery-ahead-of-emirates-nba-cup/",
      "title": "Emirates introduces bold NBA livery ahead of Emirates NBA Cup (press release, 18 October 2024)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-22",
      "note": "A6-EOD, nose to tail, painted in-house in 19 days; a blue fuselage with the NBA logo and a bouncing basketball, the Emirates lettering in red instead of gold, red engines with the calligraphy in white. Read through Business Wire's copy and AirlineGeeks."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A6-EOD_NCE_(54917538991).jpg",
      "title": "A6-EOD NCE (Eric Salard, CC BY-SA 4.0)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-22",
      "note": "Right side, taxiing at Nice, level, 2025-11-11 (the newest open photo): flipped nose-left and fitted to shapes/A388.json (nose, tail, fin tip, the first and last main-deck doors; within 24 px, about 1 m). Everything measured on it."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A6-EOD_JFK_Push_Back_From_Gate7_At_IAT_EK_A380_861_Official_Airline_Partner_Of_The_NBA_Small_(54091403066).png",
      "title": "A6-EOD JFK Push Back ... Official Airline Partner Of The NBA (Mark Bess, CC BY-SA 2.0)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-22",
      "note": "Right side from above at JFK, 2024-10-24, a week after the unveiling: the same layout; the third line 'of the NBA' (hidden by the wing at Nice) and the colours in sunlight."
    }
