  "notes": "Measured on the right side only (Nice, 2025-11-11, flipped; the JFK photo of 2024-10-24 agrees); no open photo of the left side, which is taken to be the same layout with the logo, ball and lettering in the same places. The blue is a gradient on the aircraft (darker toward the belly, brighter toward the nose in sunlight), drawn as one blue; the fine pin-stripes in it aren't drawn. The belly isn't seen in either photo: drawn blue, with no belly title. The red sweep is the A380s' (as measured on A6-EVG); here a thin white line separates it from the blue. The NBA logo and the basketball are the league's marks carried as a sponsor's: proposed as our own simplified marks (UAE/nba-logoman, UAE/nba-bounce), not traced. Status: the newest open photo is 2025-11-11; a JetPhotos photo (lead only) has it at JFK on 2025-12-11 and Emirates' 2026 special-livery round-ups still list it; no repaint reported.",
  "history": "A6-EOD flew in the 1999 flag-tail scheme until it was repainted nose to tail for the NBA in October 2024."
}
